---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const site = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_SITE_URL || "https://crosswordmaker.app";
const title = "Prizm Maker Crossword Clue — Answer GEO (3 Letters)";
const description =
  "The crossword clue “Prizm maker” is GEO — the former GM brand behind the Geo Prizm. See why, then make a printable car or geography crossword.";
const path = "/prizm-maker-crossword-clue/";

const faqs = [
  {
    q: "What is the answer to the Prizm maker crossword clue?",
    a: "GEO. It is a 3-letter fill for the former General Motors brand that sold the Prizm compact.",
  },
  {
    q: "Why is GEO the Prizm maker?",
    a: "Geo was GM’s badge for the Prizm from the 1989 through 1997 model years. Constructors use the marque name, not the Toyota plant that assembled the car.",
  },
  {
    q: "Is “former Prizm maker” a different clue?",
    a: "No. “Former Prizm maker” is the same 3-letter fill: GEO. The wording flags that the Geo brand is gone; Chevrolet sold later Prizms after Geo folded.",
  },
  {
    q: "Could Toyota or Chevrolet be the answer?",
    a: "Not for the usual 3-letter American crossword. Toyota helped build Prizms at NUMMI, and Chevrolet sold the car after 1997, but published puzzles treat Prizm maker as GEO.",
  },
  {
    q: "How do I make a crossword with clues like this?",
    a: "Use Topic mode for a car-history or geography prompt, or paste a word list (GEO, PRIZM, METRO, COROLLA) and write short definition clues. The program builds the grid; you edit every clue before print.",
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonicalPath={path}
  jsonLd={[
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "WebPage",
      name: title,
      description,
      url: `${site}${path}`,
      inLanguage: "en",
      isPartOf: { "@type": "WebSite", name: "AI Crossword Maker", url: site },
    },
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: `${site}/` },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Blog", item: `${site}/blog/` },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 3,
          name: "Prizm maker crossword clue",
          item: `${site}${path}`,
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: faqs.map((f) => ({
        "@type": "Question",
        name: f.q,
        acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: f.a },
      })),
    },
  ]}
>
  <article class="container section prose" style="padding-top:1.5rem;">
    <nav class="muted" style="font-size:0.9rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">
      <a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/blog/">Blog</a> / Prizm maker crossword clue
    </nav>
    <h1>Prizm Maker Crossword Clue</h1>
    <p>
      The standard American crossword answer for <strong>Prizm maker</strong> is
      <strong>GEO</strong> (3 letters). Geo was General Motors’ short-lived marque;
      the Prizm compact wore that badge through the 1997 model year.
    </p>

    <div
      style="border:1px solid var(--color-border);background:var(--color-surface);border-radius:8px;padding:1rem 1.1rem;margin:1.1rem 0 1.4rem;"
    >
      <p style="margin:0 0 0.35rem;font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--color-muted);">Crossword fill</p>
      <p style="margin:0;font-size:2rem;font-family:var(--font-display);letter-spacing:0.12em;">GEO</p>
      <p style="margin:0.4rem 0 0;">
        Clue: Prizm maker · Length: 3 letters · Close variant: former Prizm maker
      </p>
    </div>

    <p>
      This is a crossword <em>maker</em>, not a daily puzzle desk. We published this FAQ
      because people search the clue, then often want to write similar marque or geography
      clues for a class worksheet.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/ai-crossword-maker/"><strong>Open the AI crossword maker</strong></a>
      — free topic preview, no signup wall — or
      <a href="/crossword-maker-from-word-list/">paste a word list</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Why the answer is GEO</h2>
    <p>
      Geo launched as GM’s import-fighting brand for the 1989 model year and disappeared
      after 1997, when remaining models moved under Chevrolet. The Geo Prizm was a compact
      built at NUMMI in Fremont, California — a GM–Toyota joint plant — and shared its
      bones with the Toyota Corolla. Chevrolet sold a Prizm for a few more years
      (1998–2002), which is why later puzzles say <strong>former</strong> Prizm maker.
    </p>
    <p>
      Constructors like GEO because it is a clean 3-letter fill. “Prizm maker” points at
      the badge on the car, not the Toyota factory that assembled it. Other Geo nameplates
      you may see in the same puzzle family include Metro, Storm, and Tracker.
    </p>
    <p class="muted" style="font-size:0.92rem;">
      Crossword databases commonly list this fill in the New York Times (6 October 1999)
      and USA Today (28 December 2006). We are not a complete puzzle archive, and we do
      not mark this page as fact-verified encyclopedia copy.
    </p>

    <h2>Close wording you may have in the grid</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Prizm maker</strong> / <strong>Prizm maker crossword clue</strong> → GEO</li>
      <li><strong>Former Prizm maker</strong> → GEO (same length, same brand)</li>
      <li><strong>Prizm maker, 3 letters</strong> → GEO</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      If your squares are longer than three letters, you are probably looking at a
      different clue. Do not force TOYOTA or CHEVROLET into a 3-letter slot.
    </p>

    <h2>How to write clues like this (then print)</h2>
    <p>
      Short definition clues work better in a classroom grid than trivia riddles.
      “GM brand that sold the Prizm” is clearer for students than an obscure year-or-plant
      gag. Keep answers A–Z only; skip digits and punctuation.
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>
        Start from a topic such as “1990s cars for grade 8” in
        <a href="/ai-crossword-maker/">AI Topic mode</a>, or paste terms in
        <a href="/crossword-maker-from-word-list/">word-list mode</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        Edit every AI draft. Clues are not labeled fact-verified; shorten leaks and swap
        any word that does not fit the lesson.
      </li>
      <li>
        Click Build grid. Layout reshuffles do not spend another AI credit.
        <a href="/how-it-works/">How AI vs the grid engine works</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        Export a student PDF plus answer key from
        <a href="/printable-crossword-maker/">printable crossword maker</a>.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      Geography classes can treat GEO as a prefix (geography, geology) instead of a car
      brand — see
      <a href="/blog/how-to-make-a-geography-vocabulary-crossword/">how to make a geography vocabulary crossword</a>
      and ready printables for
      <a href="/examples/map-skills/">map skills</a>,
      <a href="/examples/world-capitals/">world capitals</a>, and
      <a href="/examples/us-states/">US states</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Related guides</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/blog/how-to-make-a-crossword-puzzle/">How to make a crossword puzzle</a></li>
      <li>
        <a href="/blog/how-to-make-a-geography-vocabulary-crossword/">Geography vocabulary crossword</a>
      </li>
      <li><a href="/blog/how-to-print-crossword-worksheets/">How to print crossword worksheets</a></li>
      <li><a href="/examples/">Examples library</a> · <a href="/blog/">How-to blog</a></li>
    </ul>
  </article>

  <section class="container section faq" style="padding-top:0;">
    <h2 class="section-title">FAQ</h2>
    {
      faqs.map((f) => (
        <details>
          <summary>{f.q}</summary>
          <p style="margin:0.6rem 0 0;">{f.a}</p>
        </details>
      ))
    }
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
